DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The vvmm__mmaapp__ssttaacckk() function maps a process stack for a new process image.
     The stack is mapped _a_d_d_r_b_o_s in _m_a_p, with a maximum size of _m_a_x___s_s_i_z_e.
     Copy-on-write flags passed in _c_o_w are also applied to the new mapping.
     Protection bits are supplied by _p_r_o_t and _m_a_x.

     It is typically called by execve(2).

     The vvmm__mmaapp__ggrroowwssttaacckk() function is responsible for growing a stack for
     the process _p to the desired address _a_d_d_r, similar to the legacy sbrk(2)
     call.

